From: MayteraOS browser engine port
Subject: [libhubbub] gate the per-token treebuilder mode printf (#245)

hubbub_treebuilder_token_handler() prints its insertion-mode name via printf on
every token. Upstream enables that whenever NDEBUG is undefined, and no
MayteraOS build script defines NDEBUG, so it shipped ON. On MayteraOS one
printf character costs a SYS_PUTCHAR syscall, a busy-wait on the 0x3F8 UART and
a syslog ring entry, so a 1,000,090-byte page spent 133,880 ms of a 362,880 ms
load emitting "IN_BODY" to the serial port.

Gated on its own opt-in macro (-DHUBBUB_DEBUG_MODES) rather than by defining
NDEBUG, because NDEBUG would also disable every assert() in all five NetSurf
libraries.

Applies to libhubbub at pin 6651b8cf87a4aa87bcdb2ff024a02659cd3f9402.
---
--- a/src/treebuilder/treebuilder.c
+++ b/src/treebuilder/treebuilder.c
@@ -213,13 +213,23 @@
 	assert((signed) treebuilder->context.current_node >= 0);
 
 /* A slightly nasty debugging hook, but very useful */
-#ifdef NDEBUG
-# define mode(x) \
-		case x:
-#else
+/* MAYTERAOS LOCAL PATCH (#245) - the ONLY change in this vendored file.
+ * Upstream leaves this printf ENABLED whenever NDEBUG is undefined, and no
+ * MayteraOS build script defines NDEBUG. It runs once per parsed token, and on
+ * this platform one printf character costs a SYS_PUTCHAR syscall, a busy-wait
+ * on the 0x3F8 UART and a 128-byte syslog ring entry, so a 1MB page spent
+ * minutes emitting insertion-mode names to the serial port instead of parsing.
+ * Gate it on its own opt-in macro: the diagnostic still exists (rebuild the
+ * engine with -DHUBBUB_DEBUG_MODES to get it back) but is OFF by default.
+ * Deliberately NOT fixed by defining NDEBUG, because that would also silently
+ * disable every assert() in all five NetSurf libraries. */
+#if defined(HUBBUB_DEBUG_MODES) && !defined(NDEBUG)
 # define mode(x) \
 		case x: \
 			printf( #x "\n");
+#else
+# define mode(x) \
+		case x:
 #endif
 
 	while (err == HUBBUB_REPROCESS) {
